      "id": 224076,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-07T21:37:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>While listening to this episode, I remembered how much C&amp;A (Adam in particular) want a fighting game based on Sentinels, and thought how Uncontrollable Flock would be a perfect special attack in a game like Marvel vs. Capcom.&nbsp; Then I remembered Setback and his goose, and got the mental image of Harpy opening a portal, unleashing a stream of birds that does a 50+ hit combo, and finishes with this goose that comes out and whacks the opponent a few times.&nbsp; Then I thought it would be even more hilarious if there was like a 5% chance that instead of the goose, you get a guy in a chicken costume that combos the opponent with a spinning fried chicken sign.</p>\n<p>Although in some ways I feel like Harpy has the same problem as Setback (they're supposed to want to balance high and low birds/Unluck but in practice you often just want them to be high), I do feel like they captured Harpy's frustration well in the game.&nbsp; I always start off trying to be careful and take advantage of high magic, and inevitably end up saying, \"Eh, this is too hard.&nbsp; F* it, BIRDS!\"</p>\n<p><strong>Edit:</strong>&nbsp;Oh, and regarding their idea that there be a superhero/supervillain named The Pupil who was a giant eyeball: let's not forget that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_(Centaur_Publications)\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">it's been done</a>.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:22.462Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
