      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>While listening to this episode, I remembered how much C&amp;A (Adam in particular) want a fighting game based on Sentinels, and thought how Uncontrollable Flock would be a perfect special attack in a game like Marvel vs. Capcom.&nbsp; Then I remembered Setback and his goose, and got the mental image of Harpy opening a portal, unleashing a stream of birds that does a 50+ hit combo, and finishes with this goose that comes out and whacks the opponent a few times.&nbsp; Then I thought it would be even more hilarious if there was like a 5% chance that instead of the goose, you get a guy in a chicken costume that combos the opponent with a spinning fried chicken sign.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although in some ways I feel like Harpy has the same problem as Setback (they're supposed to want to balance high and low birds/Unluck but in practice you often just want them to be high), I do feel like they captured Harpy's frustration well in the game.&nbsp; I always start off trying to be careful and take advantage of high magic, and inevitably end up saying, \"Eh, this is too hard.&nbsp; F* it, BIRDS!\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Edit:</strong>&nbsp;Oh, and regarding their idea that there be a superhero/supervillain named The Pupil who was a giant eyeball: let's not forget that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_(Centaur_Publications)\">it's been done</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
