    {
      "id": 224078,
      "name": "TheBazaarClerk",
      "username": "TheBazaarClerk",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thebazaarclerk/{size}/2156_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-08T13:36:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I actually prefer to stay high magic most of the time, unleashing the birds once in a while for big bursts of damage and then working&nbsp;on getting those tokens back to purple&nbsp;(I mostly play Darkwatch Harpy, so this might be a thing).&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>On the episode itself:&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-I really liked that bit on magic, how you need a well defined sense of self to avoid being manipulated&nbsp;by magical things (and also to get your elf right). Makes magic feel more esoteric and personal.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Gonna take a good while before I get used to all these characters changing names (plus some alternate universes). At least we don't have to differentiate Heritage and Legacy from Legacy and Beacon anymore, what with them being dead and all.</p>\n<p>-Not a fan of Harpmist. Mentor/Student romances are really not my thing.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Harpy had one of my favorite arcs in SoTM, from spoiled edgelord who went on to regret her life choices, to student who barely managed to control her power, and \"ending\"&nbsp;as a vital part in the battle for the multiverse. Now to see how she'll deal with her new job.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:22.624Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
