    {
      "id": 224081,
      "name": "Jeysie",
      "username": "Jeysie",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-11-12T14:22:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>TheBazaarClerk wrote:</b>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not a fan of Harpmist. Mentor/Student romances are really not my thing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>They are also super unethical, super problematic, and super counterproductive to the whole mentoring thing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Eh, I admit I don’t see this&nbsp;as a general rule. I had initially assumed it was just a matter of one adult teaching another adult a skill the second adult happened to not already know, which isn’t a problematic power differential. She certainly has spent time also teaching Argent about magic and they pretty clearly have a peer relationship.</p>\n<p>But this episode definitely cast more of a mom-like aspect of Nightmist and her teaching Harpy to be a better <em>adult</em> in addition to teaching her&nbsp;magic&nbsp;which hadn’t been apparent before, which does change&nbsp;things.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:22.844Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
