      "raw": "[quote=\"Trajector\"]\n\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>TheBazaarClerk wrote:</b>\n\n<blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">\n\nNot a fan of Harpmist. Mentor/Student romances are really not my thing.\n\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n\nThey are also super unethical, super problematic, and super counterproductive to the whole mentoring thing.\n\n[/quote]\n\nEh, I admit I don't see this&nbsp;as a general rule. I had initially assumed it was just a matter of one adult teaching another adult a skill the second adult happened to not already know, which isn't a problematic power differential. She certainly has spent time also teaching Argent about magic and they pretty clearly have a peer relationship.\n\nBut this episode definitely cast more of a mom-like aspect of Nightmist and her teaching Harpy to be a better <em>adult</em> in addition to teaching her&nbsp;magic&nbsp;which hadn't been apparent before, which does change&nbsp;things.\n",
